7736,"Irregular activity alert!
Dear Customer, During our investigation we have identified a Client Card transaction that we believe is not yours. To better protect you against fraud, were now using an Online Identification System to minimize any inconvenience to you. We have not fully restricted your account, but you must confirm your identity in order to avoid any suspension. For your security, Please Click Here to confirm your identity. As part of our security checks we'll ask you for some personal details. When more than one person is concerned, we may need to confirm the name and address of each of you. If we are unable to verify your identity electronically, your online banking will be disabled until father verification is completed at your home branch. You will be told during the identification process which options are available to you. For your protection, transactions on your account may be limited until you are able to confirm your identity. We realize that this precaution may cause you some inconvenience; however keeping your account safe is one of our top priorities. Sincerely, Sophie GouletAccount Security Representative Royal Bank of Canada Royal Bank of Canada, 2011Privacy camp; Security | Legal | Accessibility | Contact Us",d07,Business Services and Partnerships,"GENERAL SETTINGS
